  {
    "id": "wh-383744",
    "source": "wowhead",
    "dateRaw": "Wed, 04 Nov 2026 15:30:48 -0600",
    "author": "Wowhead Staff",
    "category": "Live",
    "badgeColor": "border-amber-500/60 bg-amber-950/80 text-amber-300",
    "title": {
      "en": "The Questie Addon is Back in WoW: Forever",
      "es": "El complemento Questie está de vuelta en WoW: Forever"
    },
    "summary": {
      "en": "The Questie Addon is Back in WoW: Forever...",
      "es": "El complemento Questie está de vuelta en WoW: Forever..."
    },
    "contentHtml": "\n            <div id=\"news-post-6aebc546556950.19002520\" data-insert-ads=\"article\" data-zaf-dynamic=\"article\" data-units-dynamic=\"article\" data-zaf-slot=\"true\">As we head into the launch of World of Warcraft: Forever, the thing that will occupy most of our time for the foreseeable future is leveling our characters out in the new and improved Azeroth! <br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><a class=\"wh-button zam-button\" href=\"https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questie\" data-style=\"cta\" data-variation=\"undefined\"><span class=\"wh-button-text body-text zam-button-text\" data-text-style=\"body-small-bold\" data-markup-content-target=\"1\">Download Questie Addon on CurseForge</span></a></div><br><br>While some people may follow leveling guides, others want to completely avoid any type of outside help to experience the world anew, as close to \"original\" as possible. Some players, however, may find themselves somewhere in the middle of those two camps, and for those people we can highly recommend the addon Questie.  <br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><a href=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1307229.jpg\" id=\"1307229\"><img width=\"600\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1307229.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"content-image border\" alt=\"questie example\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; aspect-ratio: 1.54114 / 1; border-width: 2px;\"></a></div><br><br>If you played Classic in 2019 (and beyond), the Questie addon is likely a well-known name to you, as the base game didn't have any type of quest indicators like the ones introduced in Wrath of the Lich King. <br><br>In Forever, the game, even without addons, has this type of feature, so Questie is more about some of the quality-of-life aspects that it improves. For example:<ul class=\"exclude-units\"><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">Providing Quest indicators on the map for quests you don't currently have in your log, so that you don't miss new quests.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">Additional data points for quest drops on the map.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">Party announcement on quest completions</div></li></ul>... and more! <br><br>On the beta, there were a lot of quests that were improperly tracked through the in-game system, and quests that are easy to miss, even on a first, second, or third playthrough. So, if you want to fully experience all the new content without having your hand held by a leveling guide, then Questie might be a good addition to your addon folder this launch!<br><br>If you want to download the addon, you can find it in any of the addon management apps or on CurseForge.com.</div>\n            \n            <noscript>As we head into the launch of World of Warcraft: Forever, the thing that will occupy most of our time for the foreseeable future is leveling our characters out in the new and improved Azeroth! <br /><br />Download Questie Addon on CurseForge<br /><br />While some people may follow leveling guides, others want to completely avoid any type of outside help to experience the world anew, as close to &quot;original&quot; as possible. Some players, however, may find themselves somewhere in the middle of those two camps, and for those people we can highly recommend the addon Questie. <br /><br />If you played Classic in 2019 (and beyond), the Questie addon is likely a well-known name to you, as the base game didn't have any type of quest indicators like the ones introduced in Wrath of the Lich King. <br /><br />In Forever, the game, even without addons, has this type of feature, so Questie is more about some of the quality-of-life aspects that it improves. For example: <br /><ul><li>Providing Quest indicators on the map for quests you don't currently have in your log, so that you don't miss new quests.</li><li>Additional data points for quest drops on the map.</li><li>Party announcement on quest completions</li></ul><br />... and more! <br /><br />On the beta, there were a lot of quests that were improperly tracked through the in-game system, and quests that are easy to miss, even on a first, second, or third playthrough. So, if you want to fully experience all the new content without having your hand held by a leveling guide, then Questie might be a good addition to your addon folder this launch!<br /><br />If you want to download the addon, you can find it in any of the addon management apps or on CurseForge.com.</noscript>            \n        ",
    "imageUrl": "https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/blog/images/56012-the-questie-addon-is-back-in-wow-forever.jpg",
